  "body": "Held and cherished by the original owner, this architect-designed, builder's own residence is now being offered to the market. The architect's brief was simple: a view from every room. Almost three decades later you have a unique opportunity to secure the home that delivered so beautifully on its brief.\r\nElevated above shimmering blue waters, this extraordinary residence enjoys breathtaking views across the harbour to Rangitoto and the islands of the Hauraki Gulf.  From sunrise coffee to exceptional evening entertaining, this is your perfect setting for creating unforgettable memories together.\r\nSet on 957sqm of land (more or less), with approximately 319sqm of versatile living, there is space here for families to grow, gather and retreat. Four bedrooms, two bathrooms, a powder room and three generous living areas provide flexibility for changing needs.\r\nThe second living zone is particularly versatile, with its own wet bar / kitchenette, spacious lounge and dining space, separate entrance and deck overlooking Rangitoto. It could comfortably accommodate multigenerational living, overseas guests, work-from-home separation, fabulous mancave, games room or an independent boarder.\r\nDecks extend from multiple sides of the home, allowing you to follow the sun, changing light and views throughout the day. With north-facing street appeal, the home enjoys all-day sunshine, some of the Shore's widest eastern coastal views and a restful outlook over the bush and valley to the south.\r\nThe neighbouring bush reserve is also being upgraded with a network of walking tracks and glades, to allow you to access this natural setting more easily.\r\nDesigned to celebrate its landmark position, multiple feature windows draw light deep into the home, creating bright, uplifting spaces by day and a sparkling display of light to the street at night.\r\nSought-after school zones include Glamorgan Primary, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College.\r\nWhen the sun rises over Rangitoto, reflected in the harbour below, you'll understand why this home has been treasured for nearly three decades. Our vendors will certainly find it difficult to leave, but the time has come for its next owners to make their own memories here.\r\nWe invite you to experience, for yourself, the outlook you'll love waking up to every day.",
